/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  Benchmark C -- topology.  One counter-current extractor of 4 equilibrium
  stages: the aqueous feed enters stage 1, the MIBK solvent stage 4; the
  extract leaves stage 1, the raffinate stage 4 -- the same arrangement as
  the reference sample (feed on its Stage0, solvent on its Stage3, extract
  overhead, raffinate as bottoms).

  THIS RUN IS NOT AN ANSWER TODAY.  Measured 2026-10-20: the `extractor`
  publishes `converged 0` with its mass closure off by 23 % (NRTL) and 50 %
  (UNIFAC), at exit 0 -- its per-stage liquid-liquid flash returns one
  liquid on feeds an independent stability test finds strongly unstable
  (README, "Findings on Choupo's side").  The case is kept as the problem
  POSED, so the comparison shows the answer the day the engine gives one;
  variants/stageCascade is the same cascade written out as four flashes
  and four mixers, which fails the same way.

  ONE DIFFERENCE IN THE PROBLEM, stated: Choupo's `extractor` is ISOTHERMAL
  (src/unitOperations/separation/Extractor.H, "EXPLICIT ASSUMPTIONS"); the
  reference column is adiabatic and its stages cool from 296.54 K to
  284.70 K.  The column here runs at the feeds' 298.15 K.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        extractor;
        type        extractor;
        inputs      ( feed  solvent );        // feed at stage 1, solvent at stage N
        outputs     ( extract  raffinate );   // extract leaves stage 1, raffinate stage N

        operation
        {
            stages       4;
            solvent      methylIsobutylKetone;   // defines the extract phase
            temperature  298.15 K;               // the feeds' temperature (isothermal model)
        }
    }
);
